WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.655
By the end of this module you should be able to
choose

00:00:02.682 --> 00:00:06.566
a join type based on the question rather than by
habit You

00:00:06.592 --> 00:00:10.026
should be able to explain what rows are preserved
what rows require

00:00:10.053 --> 00:00:13.342
a match and where NULL values can appear after an
outer join

00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:20.493
You will also practice writing explicit join
conditions with table aliases When

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:23.901
two tables contain a column with the same name
aliases make it

00:00:23.914 --> 00:00:28.946
clear which table the column comes from A major
learning goal is

00:00:28.959 --> 00:00:33.870
protecting the grain Grain means what one row in the
result represents

00:00:34.777 --> 00:00:38.199
A patient table may have one row per patient while
an admissions

00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:42.475
table may have several rows for the same patient
When those tables

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:48.262
are joined repeated patient rows may be completely
correct Finally

00:00:48.498 --> 00:00:52.527
you should be able to validate a join A query
running without

00:00:52.554 --> 00:00:56.988
an error does not prove that the result is
analytically correct We

00:00:57.001 --> 00:01:01.751
will check counts distinct identifiers unmatched
rows and a few known records
